SECTION C -- the enumerated evading structures, each against every obstruction
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    C1: the flux route.  With one order parameter q: a0 = beta sqrt(G) q, rho_vac c^2 = Z~ q^2/2, Z~ = Z + 2 b beta^2.
        kappa^2 = a0^2/(G eps) = 2*beta**2/(Z + 2*b*beta**2): q CANCELS (the LOCK holds on the amplitude direction, A6/M3),
        and kappa is the ratio 2 beta^2/Z~ -- one number that no equation of the flux sector fixes (k04 F2, L3 Q5).
        canonically normalising (q -> q'/sqrt(Z~)) leaves ONE invariant, beta/sqrt(Z~) = kappa/sqrt(2) = 0.3536 (canonical footing):
        kappa IS the dimensionless coupling of the MOND sector to the canonically normalised vacuum order parameter.
  [FAIL] C1 [flux] the conserved-flux route supplies RIGIDITY as well as the LOCK (i.e. the coefficient as well as the form)   (it supplies the LOCK only.  Generalised statement of L3's theorem: every quantity the cosmological/membrane sector can measure is a function of Z~ alone, because Z~ is the full stiffness of the order parameter; beta is a coupling of the SAME order parameter to a different sector, and no equation of the first sector can see it.  OBSTRUCTION O2 (split degeneracy), generic to (m, n) = (2, 1).)
    C2: any global constraint that fixes a scale by a SPACETIME AVERAGE of the MOND Lagrangian.
        t0 = 13.80 Gyr; H_Lambda^-1 = 17.53 Gyr; a(10 t0) = 1.192e+03 (7.1 e-folds)
        <L>_(to t0) / L(today) = 1.8964;  <L>_(to 10 t0) / L(today) = 2.077e-08;  ratio future/now = 1.095e-08
  [FAIL] C2 [global] a 4-volume-averaged global constraint (sequestering type) retains a non-vanishing MOND contribution into the de Sitter future   (it does not: the average to 10 t0 is 1.1e-08 of the average to t0 (k02 reports 1e-8 for its own weighting).  THEOREM T3, general: in a Lambda-dominated future the 4-volume grows as e^(3 H_Lambda t) while the peculiar field freezes and its Lagrangian density per comoving volume tends to a constant, so ANY 4-volume average of a gradient sector is driven to zero.  This closes the whole global-constraint class, not only sequestering -- and independently of the 1e5 magnitude miss of k02.)
    C3: a boundary or horizon term.  On a homogeneous isotropic background the MOND gradient invariant is
        Y = q^mn d_m phi d_n phi = 0 IDENTICALLY (homogeneity), so the MOND sector sits at Y = 0 everywhere on
        the background and carries no boundary data at the cosmological horizon.
        the only survivor of the MOND sector at the horizon is J(0), the very constant T1 shows is degenerate with Lambda: lim_(Y->0) [J(Y) - J(0)] = 0
  [FAIL] C3 [boundary] a horizon/boundary term can see the MOND sector, i.e. the MOND gradient invariant is nonzero on the homogeneous background   (it is identically zero.  THEOREM T4: the MOND sector is a GRADIENT sector; a homogeneous background sets its invariant to zero; the only quantity it can hand a boundary term is J(0), which T1 has already shown to be pure cosmological constant.  This is why L3's Q9 (GHY) and Q10 (Brown-York) both returned functions of the total stiffness alone -- the result is structural, not a feature of that model.)
    C4: an anomaly.  Anomaly-induced terms are built from curvature invariants (Riegert/Polyakov); A4 shows every
        such invariant is an integer power of Lambda on de Sitter, i.e. an EVEN power of a mass scale.  Excluded by T5.
    C5: an RG fixed point needs running, and running needs propagating modes.  A p-form in D dimensions carries
        C(D-2, p) physical polarisations: 3-form in D = 4 -> 0 (Duff-van Nieuwenhuizen), 1-form -> 2 (photon).
  [FAIL] C5 [RG] the order-parameter sector of the flux route has propagating degrees of freedom, so its stiffness can run to a fixed point   (a 3-form gauge field in D = 4 has 0 propagating modes, so Z~ receives no loop correction from its own sector and cannot flow to a fixed point that would fix Z~/beta^2.  CAVEAT stated: matter loops can still renormalise Z~ if the four-form couples to charged matter, and that has NOT been computed here -- an RG fixed point in a DIFFERENT sector remains formally open.)
    C6: horizon thermodynamics gives the identification a0 = c^2/(2 pi L_dS), i.e. kappa = sqrt(8pi/3)/(2pi) = 0.4607
        (8.5% from 1/2).  It satisfies the LOCK (both scales from the same horizon) and it is the one
        principle-shaped coefficient k03 could not exclude -- but it is an IDENTIFICATION of a0 with a horizon temperature scale,
        not a consequence of field equations, and k03 shows it is degenerate with the H0 tension to 0.2%.
    C7: dimensional transmutation in a strongly coupled sector: a0 = mu exp(-1/(b g^2)) with rho_vac the square of the
        same condensate satisfies A4/(m,n) = (2,1) and the LOCK automatically, and kappa becomes a ratio of two condensates
        in ONE theory -- a non-perturbatively computable pure number.  Not excluded by T1-T6; not attempted anywhere in the corpus.
    C8: a nonlinearly realised symmetry (coset/Goldstone).  This is the ONLY enumerated structure that could supply RIGIDITY:
        in a coset construction the linear coupling of the order parameter to an external sector and the quadratic stiffness of
        the same order parameter are BOTH fixed by one breaking scale and by the coset's curvature, so beta/sqrt(Z~) becomes a
        group-theoretic number.  Not excluded by T1-T6; not attempted anywhere in the corpus.

    C9: the exclusion matrix (structure -> obstruction that closes it):
        S1 local action, a0 a Lagrangian constant        EXCLUDED by T1
        S2 conserved flux / four-form (k04, L3)          EXCLUDED by T2
        S3 global 4-volume constraint (sequestering)     EXCLUDED by T3
        S4 boundary / GHY / Brown-York                   EXCLUDED by T4
        S5 anomaly / curvature invariants                EXCLUDED by T5
        S6 RG fixed point of the flux stiffness          EXCLUDED by T6
        S7 unimodular / two-measure                      EXCLUDED by T1*
        S8 horizon thermodynamics (identification)       OPEN -- no known obstruction applies
        S9 dimensional transmutation, two condensates    OPEN -- no known obstruction applies
        S10 nonlinear realisation / coset                OPEN -- no known obstruction applies
        T1* = the additive freedom is converted into an undetermined integration constant, not removed (B3 (ii)).
  [PASS] C9 [verdict] at least one enumerated structure evades every known obstruction   (3 do: S8 horizon thermodynamics (identification), S9 dimensional transmutation, two condensates, S10 nonlinear realisation / coset.  7 of the 10 are closed by a theorem stated here in general form (S7 only weakly: the freedom is relocated, not removed).)

