        3/(4+pi) = 0.4201, 3/7 = 0.4286, e/(2pi) = 0.4326, 4/9 = 0.4444, 5/11 = 0.4545, 1/(2pi) x sqrt(8pi/3) = 0.4607, 3/(2pi) = 0.4775, 1/2 = 0.5000, sqrt(2)/e = 0.5203, pi/6 = 0.5236, e/5 = 0.5437, 6/11 = 0.5455, 5/9 = 0.5556, sqrt(5)/4 = 0.5590, 1/sqrt(pi) = 0.5642, pi/2 - 1 = 0.5708, 4/7 = 0.5714, 1/sqrt(3) = 0.5774 ...
    D3: inside the 3-sigma band WITH the H0 convention [0.402, 0.658]: 29 of them
  [FAIL] D3 [guard] the measured band is discriminating: at most 3 simple 'principle-shaped' numbers lie inside it, so a theory landing there would be evidence   (27 lie inside the statistical band and 29 inside the band with the H0 convention.  Landing in the band is therefore NOT evidence for a mechanism; only the DERIVATION can be evidence.  This is the numerology guard for every future candidate: quote the derivation, never the proximity.)
    D4: to be REJECTABLE at 3 sigma a prediction must differ from 0.530 by more than 24%; 1/2 differs by 5.7% and the horizon value 0.4607 by 13.1% -- neither is rejectable
    D4: after canonical normalisation kappa/sqrt(2) = 0.3536 (canonical) / 0.4259 (alt) is a
        dimensionless coupling of order unity.  There is no naturalness problem to solve -- and equally no dynamical reason for the
        value.  The structures known to FIX a dimensionless coupling are: a gauge charge (integer), a Wess-Zumino-Witten level
        (integer), an index/anomaly coefficient (rational/16 pi^2), and a coset normalisation (group-theoretic).  L3 closed the
        gauge-charge route for this sector (beta multiplies the field strength, not the potential; a 2-brane in D = 4 has no
        magnetic partner).  The other three have not been tried.

